Hi,

I'm trying to install Debian GNU/Linux Woody/Alpha on my XL266.
Unfortunately, I can't even get the installer loaded.

After trying dozens different MILOs (the XL ist ARC only), I found a working
one (2.0.30). I then tried to get the CD at

  http://www.phy.olemiss.edu/debian-cd/

to boot with

  MILO> boot scd0:/boot/linux root=/dev/scd0 load_ramdisk=1

but all I got was "Unable to mount root fs". After that, I tried the
floppies at

  ftp://ftp.de.debian.org/debian/dists/woody/main/disks-alpha/3.0.23-2002-05-21/images-1.44/

with

  MILO> boot fd0:/linux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1

The first disk (rescue) boots just fine and then prompts to insert the root
disk, but then, all I get is

  RAMDISK: Couldn't find valid RAM disk image starting at 0.

There is a valid compressed ext2 fs on this disk.

After that and also without load_ramdisk=1 I get

  VFS: INsert root floppy and press ENTER

followed by

  Kernel panic: VFS: Unable to mount root fs on 02:00

This isn't surprising, as this disk contains a _compressed image_.

Did anyone here succeed installing Debian/GNU Linux Woody on an XL or any
other system with ARC? If so, what did you do?
Any suggestions?

TIA, Bodo
