Just for a little clarification on the boot sequence for alpha.

type the following:
 >>> set bootdef_dev dka0
 >>> set auto_action BOOT
 >>> set boot_osflags 0
as an option you may also set:
 >>> set boot_reset ON
This will force the machine to reboot before booting from dka0 for a 
clean startup.

I just thought I would clear this up since you cannot set a value to 
boot_dev directly. If you would like to see the results of these 
settings type:
 >>> show boot*
this will list all variables starting with "boot" of course. For more 
info on SRM go to HP's site and find the user manual PDF for your 
machine. Compaq has archives most of the Digital branded Alpha manuals 
under retired servers. I think you can get enough info on SRM even if 
the manual is not specifically for you machine. I am also new to alpha 
(alphaserver 1200) and the user manual is invaluable. It's worth a shot.

