So append a correct root= optione then ^__^; If you're booting from CDROM,
your root should be /dev/scd0, when booting from floppy, root should be
/dev/fd0.


>Now the current boot off the HD is the following:
>Boot file: Disk0, Partition1, \linload.exe
>OS path: Disk0, Partition3, \milo

Interesting, usually, linload.exe and milo reside on the same, FAT
formatted, partition.

>OS Options: boot sda3:vmlinux_6499b.gz root=/dev/sda3
