Are you shure, that's the boot definition you're booting? You can have four
or five boot definitions...


>2-
>Now onto other questions, when making floppies from images, is the block
>count important ? I've seen examples where it's not specified and others
>where they use bs=72k.

If you use the same blocksize as the floppy (-driver), the access could be a
bit quicker, that's all.

>3-
>How to upgrade MILO ? I've made a floppy with the latest version, but I have
>no clue what to do with it.

Boot your running Linux, find the FAT partition with your old milo and - and
this is really important! - _add_ the new milo to it with an other name.
Modify your boot definition to use the new milo instead of the old one or
add a second boot definition.

If it doesn't work, switch back to your old milo.

