Dr. David Kirkby <drkirkby@ntlworld.com> wrote:
---[search for Alpha docs]---

Unfortunately you did not say what OS(es) you develop for.  In addition
to the sites already mentioned, look at http://www.tru64.org

Be careful with Alpha workstations on ebay. _Sometimes_ you may get
one for a bargain price. More often, slow dogs sell for high prices.

If you want Tru64 Unix support, avoid the DEC3000 series. These are 
not supported by current Tru64 releases anymore, and Linux support is
not good either. (But they run NetBSD, OpenBSD and VMS just fine and
often come for free :-) And do not buy an "Alpha XL". There is no
SRM firmware for the XL, so XLs are WinNT and Linux only.

In your situation, I would look for a PWS/au series machine. They
are reasonably fast and can run all operating systems. If you have
more money at hand, an XP1000 or DS10 may be an option.

regards

Wolfgang Rupp



