> I'm trying to boot my Alpha from the RedHat 7.2 cdrom so I can perform an
> upgrade. It's an AlphaPC 164LX with MILO, Digital Alpha 21164 rev 7.2,
> AlphaBios 5.62-1a, RedHat 5.0, kernel 2.0.35

As I wrote sometime ago this WILL NOT WORK. Milo that old will not
load correctly a kernel which does not have LEGACY_LOAD_ADDRESS
in its configuration. Once again, either you need a milo which can
handle such kernels (I have no idea if it already exists for LX
but maybe), or a custom kernel with appropriate modules on boot
floppies, or switch to SRM.

> and other variants. They all lead to a:
> Please Append a correct "root=" boot option
> Kernel Panic: VFS: Unable to mount root fs on 08:02

This is exactly what is expected in the situation as described.
There could be few more failure modes but this will not fly.

It is possible to hack and get LX to work with milo applying enough
of an elbow grease but personally I would not bother and use SRM
for a firmware.  This also has some work required - in particular
a partitioning type has to be changed on a boot disk - but it will
be much less headaches on a longer run.  Decently capable milo
could be an option but you will be forever in "no supported"
situation.

  Michal


