I am not quite sure about the state of the current Debian install-CDs, but
if one of the CDs is bootable on the Jensen (using aboot), you should be
able to boot off that CD and install the system without the old ARC-based
fdisk/copyboot-Tools.

If the kernel loads from CD, you should at least be able to pass
root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1
as commandline and proceed with root/drivers from floppy disks, and then
install the packages from CD.

