>eb.ea.e9.e8.e7.e6....e5
>
>V6.9-4 built on Oct 12 1998 at 11:22:55

That's the SRM version number, I think, so you do have it installed.

>CPU 0 booting
>
>(boot dka0.0.0.6.0 -flags a)

But its autoaction variable is set to boot.  If you know the root
password to the Tru64 installation, you can use the consvar command to
set the auto_action variable to HALT, which will then get you an SRM
prompt next time you reboot.

If you don't know the root password, I suggest you open the machine,
disconnect the hard disk, and reboot.  Since the boot will then fail,
you should get an SRM prompt, at which you can type:

set auto_action HALT

and then you can power off, reconnect your hard disk, and power up to an
SRM prompt.

Tim



