It is possible to upgrade from 7.0 => 7.2 by simply upgrading individual 
packages manually (not using the installer), but you have to tip-toe through the 
dependencies.  The compatibility packages come in particularly handy and, for 
some packages, you might need to install intermediate versions from 7.1.

Rawhide is released by Red Hat rather than Compaq/HP and so is unsupported and 
probably not very tested (Red Hat no longer supports the Alpha platform).

