> 
> then, i think mine is a ZLXp-L2.
.....
> 
> but it does not work with xfree 3.3 nor 4.x

ZLXp-L<anything> are _not_ TGA cards and AFAIK they are not supported
by XFree86 at all.  OTOH ZLXp-E[123] cards are TGA, or maybe TGA2,
and these are supported at least by 4.x.  IIRC one needs to specify
explicitely BusID for that card in a "Device" section.  Something
like 
    BusID   "PCI:1:0:0"
'lspci' should provide required values.

  Michal


