Sorry about all this. However, I did find the solution to this problem. =
I noticed in /etc/modules.conf that eth0 was set as tulip. Thus I =
changed the:



alias    eth0    tulip=20

to

alias    eth0    de4x5.

Next, you need to shutdown the network, remove the tulip driver as a =
module, load the de4x5 driver as a module, and restart the network. =
Viola, the controller card is up and running.

Now, I can't telnet in but I can telnet out. I am sure that this is a =
minor configuration problem that I will figure out tomorrow.



Regards,



George

  "George Samuelson" <samuelsong@insightbb.com> wrote in message =
news:COcY9.17859$rM2.16573@rwcrnsc53...


  All,



  I have the following hardware:

  AlphaStation 200 (Avanti) Dechip 21064A-2

  80 Meg of Ram

  6 Gigs of diskspace

  SRM V6.3

  ethernet is a Decchip 21040 network controller.



  I installed Alpha Linux V7.2 successfully. However, upon bootup the =
portion where the network controller is brought on-line, IE (Starting up =
interface eth0    OK), the controller is actually shutdown. I know it is =
shutdown since the LED on the hub goes off.



  When I execute "ifconfig eth0 down" the controller will come on-line. =
However, the system thinks that all network operations are down.

  Anybody else have this problem and, if so, what is the fix?



  Regards,



  George Samuelson





