On Sun, 05 Jan 2003 22:27:45 GMT, Jim West <jcwest16@cox.net> wrote:
>Are recent builds of Mozilla available for Alpha Linux somewhere? All my
>searches seem to end up on alpha releases for Intel Linux.

In case you are willing to build from source, it isn't too
very difficult, given the size of the thing.  At least on
RH7.1, I use the following .mozconfig file for "real"
(non-debug) builds: (indentation mine)

    ac_add_options --disable-tests
    ac_add_options --disable-debug
    ac_add_options --enable-optimize
    ac_add_options --enable-crypto

I use the following command: (also, indentation mine)

    gmake -f client.mk build

Good luck.

Robert Riches
rm.riches@verizon.net


