Does anyone have any experience with any of the PCI IDE RAID controllers
on an Alpha?  I recently received an AlphaStation 400, which is rather
old and has only three PCI slots.  Two of the slots have ethernet cards
in them, so that leaves one.  I don't have or need a video card, as I
set the firmware for a serial console, which seems to work OK.  Old
SCSI drives are still expensive for their small size, when for the same
money I could toss in two IDE drive in a RAID 1 config for my /home dir.
Of course, I'd have to keep the 1 gig and 540 meg SCSI drives around for
boot, root, swap, etc.  I want to make a server out of it, cheap.  I got
RH 7.2 on it, but I would really much rather have Slackware.  If I got
the RAID controller working, then I'd have the space to let it could sit
and compile Slack-current.  Appearently, if I don't compile it myself,
who knows when it will be available for the alpha?

As a side note, I found the source code for VMS which enables the
onboard IDE port.  Can this be made to work in Linux?  Is it worth
the effort?  I flashed the firmware to the latest rev I could find,
7.2-1, but that didn't seem to enable it.

Any help will be appreciated.

Andy Johnson



